        <OtherAbstract Type="KIE" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>The guilty judgment of the Maryland Circuit Court, Monroe County, against Dr. Edward Taub, a scientific investigator, for failure to provide necessary veterinary care to research monkeys was reversed and remanded by the Court of Appeals of Maryland. The appellate court found that the state animal cruelty statute was not applicable to a research institute conducting medical and scientific research, because the act sought to punish only the &quot;unnecessary&quot; or &quot;unjustifiable&quot; infliction of pain and suffering on animals, and because Taub's facility was subject to the Federal Animal Welfare Act.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
